+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Logging and ops alerts
+
+PegaFila has three observability lanes. Pick the lane that matches the reason
+you are writing, not the severity of the message.
+
+| Lane | Channel / API | Destination | Use it for |
+| ---- | ------------- | ----------- | ---------- |
+| **Archive** | `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (`daily`) | `storage/logs/laravel.log`, rotated daily, 14 days | Routine application and framework logs: request errors, job failures, deprecations, diagnostics. |
+| **Audit** | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` (`audit`) | `storage/logs/audit.log`, rotated daily, 90 days | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail: role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts, access denials. |
+| **Alert** | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` | Discord incoming webhook | Human-pageable production incidents only: exhausted jobs, broken payment webhooks, plan limits blocking an entity. |
+
+The default `stack` points at the **archive** lane (`LOG_STACK=daily`). The
+audit channel is deliberately **not** part of the stack: write to it explicitly
+when the event needs the durable trail. Discord is deliberately **not** a
+Monolog channel; code decides when an incident is worth paging a human.
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. Is a human expected to act now? -> **Alert** (`DiscordOpsAlert`).
+2. Does this need a durable record of who changed or attempted what? -> **Audit**.
+3. Otherwise -> **Archive** (the normal `Log::` facade).
+
+Typical examples:
+
+| Event | Lane |
+| ----- | ---- |
+| Queue job exhausted all retries | Alert |
+| Asaas webhook failing repeatedly | Alert |
+| Plan limit blocks an entity from operating | Alert |
+| Membership role changed | Audit |
+| Subscription status transition | Audit |
+| Login lockout / repeated auth failure | Audit |
+| Validation error, 500 response, slow query, debug detail | Archive |
+
+An event can use more than one lane (for example, an audit entry **and** an
+alert), but keep each write intentional.
+
+## Archive
+
+Routine logs use the default channel, so no channel name is needed:
+
+```php
+Log::error('Asaas webhook rejected', ['status' => 422]);
+```
+
+Configuration: `config/logging.php` -> `channels.daily`, path
+`storage/logs/laravel.log`, level `LOG_LEVEL` (default `debug`), retention
+`LOG_DAILY_DAYS` (default `14`).
+
+## Audit
+
+Audit entries are written explicitly and should identify the actor, the entity,
+the action and the outcome — never secrets or raw personal data:
+
+```php
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'actor_id' => $user->id,
+    'entity_id' => $entity->id,
+    'from' => 'trialing',
+    'to' => 'active',
+]);
+```
+
+Configuration: `channels.audit`, path `storage/logs/audit.log`, minimum level
+`LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` (default `info`), retention `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` (default `90`).
+
+## Alerts
+
+Alerts are an explicit service call. The notifier reads
+`services.discord.webhook_url` (env `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`); when it is unset or
+empty the call is a silent no-op and no HTTP request is made.
+
+```php
+use App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert;
+
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Queue job exhausted retries',
+    'The asaas-webhooks worker failed after all retries.',
+    [
+        'queue' => 'asaas-webhooks',
+        'entity_id' => 42,
+        'job' => 'ProcessAsaasWebhook',
+    ],
+);
+```
+
+The text is the title, the message and one `key=value` line per context entry,
+truncated to 1800 characters (multibyte-safe). Context keys that look sensitive
+(`password`, `token`, `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`,
+`webhook`) and any value containing a `Bearer <credential>` are replaced with
+`[redacted]`; nested arrays are redacted recursively and rendered as JSON.
+
+Delivery is best-effort: non-2xx responses and transport errors are logged to
+the archive lane at `error` level, with the webhook URL scrubbed from the
+message. The notifier never throws. Do not use it for routine logging, and never
+put a Discord webhook behind a Monolog channel.
+
+## Environment keys
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | ------- | ------- |
+| `LOG_CHANNEL` | `stack` | Default channel. |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels in the default stack; keep the archive lane here. |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Archive minimum level. |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Audit minimum level. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days. |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty | Ops alert webhook; empty disables alerts. |
